        "The whistle case is a flat box of black iron on the kennel wall, locked with a key Ruoshui does not carry. She stands in front of it with her hands folded. No one has opened it since the night, she says, and she would rather you did not try.",
        "She lets you rest a palm against the box. It is cold, and from within comes a faint sound, the exhalation of a whistle that has been breathed into and never blown. The hounds’ ears prick as one.",
        "A guard from the sealed gate comes down to ask whether any hound has been loosed. Ruoshui opens a cage and invites him to count the occupants himself, and after a glance at the nearest he is content to take her word.",
        "The whistle was Ruoshui’s master’s, and calls a single word, and the word is a name. She heard it blown once, on the night the corridor was sealed, and the hounds went out and did not come back for seven days. She has never found out whom they were calling.",
        "At the kennel’s far end the stone is the colour of old bone, and down it runs a damp line, absurdly straight. A cold draught comes out of it, smelling of iron and distance.",
