        "The lineage chart is carved into the kennel’s back wall, a tree of names with hounds at every branch. Ruoshui lets you trace the oldest line. It ends in a symbol you almost know, a hound with its head thrown back.",
        "Each branch of the tree has a mark beside it, a dot for a hound that lived and a bar for one that did not. The bars cluster near the root, thick as a hedge, and then fall away, until the last twenty lines are dots only. Ruoshui says that is when her master learned what they were for.",
        "The hounds in their cages turn their heads as you walk the row, one after another, and a faint ringing fills the air, like a hundred sword-blades tuned to the same note. Iron answers a bright-metal root the way a tuning-fork answers a struck bell.",
